@format 1
@id queue.cancel-work
@title Cancel running work
@area 4. Queue and scheduling
@entry input
@summary Confirm cancellation of currently running items, disable automatic execution, and arm per-item cancellation; only a nonzero observed exit becomes cancelled storage.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.run-job, queue.load
@tag queue
@tag cancellation

@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias runner = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LRunner
@alias job = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LJob
@alias schedule = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSchedule

[input] User requests cancellation <input>
- Receive the Cancel command for the active station @ console.PConsoleCancelHandle(...)
> inspect

[inspect] Inspect running work <decision>
- Read all running items owned by the active station @ console.PConsoleRunningRead(...)
? "No item is running" > unchanged
? "One or more items are running" > confirm

[confirm] Confirm destructive action <decision>
- Show the running-item cancellation confirmation @ console.PConsoleCancelHandle(...)
? "User declines" > unchanged
? "User confirms" > signal

[signal] Signal every running job <process>
- Disable automatic execution for the station @ console.PConsoleCancelHandle(...)
- Arm explicit cancellation for each running work identifier @ runner.LRunnerJobCancel(...)
- Kill an already attached FFmpeg process, or kill it when it attaches @ runner.LRunnerProcessAttach(...)
> observe

[observe] Running job observes termination <decision>
- Distinguish explicit item cancellation from general runner cancellation @ job.LJobRun(...)
? "The explicit cancellation produces a nonzero process exit" > persist
? "The process exits successfully before cancellation is observed" > completed
? "The process has not reached the observable cancellation path yet" > armed

[persist] Persist restartable cancellation <storage>
- Set the finish time and request durable cancellation @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Remove partial output, move the record to cancelled storage, clear ownership, and reload the schedule @ schedule.LScheduleItemCancel(...)
> result

[armed] Cancellation armed <output>
= The job remains marked for explicit cancellation and will be terminated when its process attaches or exits.

[completed] Work completes before cancellation <output>
- Commit the zero-exit job through normal completion @ job.LJobRun(...)
= The work is stored as successful, not cancelled.

[result] Observed cancellation stored <output>
= This observed job is stored as cancelled and can be restarted; automatic execution remains disabled.

[unchanged] No cancellation <output>
= Running work and automatic-execution state are unchanged.
